meta {
  name: Suspend transfer
  type: http
  seq: 18
}

post {
  url: {{mgmtUrl}}/v1/transfers/{{mgmtTransferConsumerPid}}/suspension
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 202
  res.body.consumerPid: isDefined
}

docs {
  Suspends a STARTED transfer (added in 1.1): the provider's data plane refuses the
  token until the transfer is started again. This is the management API, not the DSP
  endpoint: it takes no body, and it answers 202 with the transfer as the connector sees
  it (the same shape as "Get transfer"). The connector then sends the DSP
  TransferSuspensionMessage to the provider in the background; the state becomes
  SUSPENDED once the provider acknowledges it. The dataAddress is kept.
  400 when the transfer is not STARTED or a message is still on its way; 404 for an
  unknown consumerPid.
}
